   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation to designating village of Lake George seasonal constables as peace officers",
    "basePrintNo": "S3496",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3496-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2.10, CP L",
    "lawSection": "Criminal Procedure Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3496\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the criminal procedure law, in relation\nto designating village of Lake George seasonal constables as peace offi-\ncers\n\nPURPOSE:  To provide peace officer status to seasonal employees of the\nVillage of Lake George who are charged with enforcement of local laws.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one - provides that employees of the village of Lake George\nemployed as seasonal village constables are hereby designated as peace\nofficers with the power to issue appearance tickets and simplified traf-\nfic informations for offenses defined in the code of the Village of Lake\nGeorge and for offenses designated to be violations in the statutes of\nthe state. These officers are further prohibited from carrying firearms\nunless appropriately licensed pursuant to Section 400.00 of the Penal\nlaw.\n\nSection two - contains the effective date.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nSection 2.10 of the Criminal Procedure Law provides for peace officer\ndesignation.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  The Village of Lake George hires 15-20 individuals each\nsummer season to patrol their streets, enforce local laws and direct\ntraffic. This seasonal program won the 2003 Local Government Achievement\nA ward and has resulted in saving the community thousands of dollars\nannually.  This legislation has been introduced at the request of the\nVillage of Lake George in order to ensure the safety of residents and\ntourists in Lake George during the busy tourist season.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: 2008: S7729-A Veto number 126\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None to the State.\n\nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  Enactment will result in annual savings of\n$400,000 to $600,000 to the Village of Lake George.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
