    "lawCode": "Amd §2.10, CP L",
    "lawSection": "Criminal Procedure Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3496A\n\nTITLE  OF  BILL:    An  act  to  amend  the criminal procedure law, in\nrelation to designating village of Lake George seasonal constables  as\npeace officers\n\nPURPOSE:  To provide peace officer status to seasonal employees of the\nVillage of Lake George who are charged with enforcement of local laws.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection  one  provides  that  employees  of the village of Lake George\nemployed as seasonal village constables are hereby designated as peace\nofficers with the power to issue  appearance  tickets  and  simplified\ntraffic  informations  for  the  offenses  defined  in the code of the\nvillage of Lake George and for offenses designated to be violations in\nthe statutes of the state  These officers are further prohibited  from\ncarrying  firearms  unless  appropriately licensed pursuant to Section\n400.00 of the penal law.\n\nSection two contains the effective date.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nSection 2.10 of the criminal procedure law provides for peace  officer\ndesignation.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:    The  village  of Lake George hires 15-20 individuals\neach summer season to patrol their streets,  enforce  local  laws  and\ndirect  traffic.  This  seasonal program won the 2003 Local Government\nAchievement award and as resulted in saving the community thousands of\ndollars annually.  This legislation has been introduced at the request\nof the village of Lake  George  in  order  to  ensure  the  safety  or\nresidents and tourists in Lake George during the busy tourist season.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:  2008: S. 7729-A Veto number 126\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None to the State\n\nLOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:  Enactment will result in annual savings of\n$400,000 to $600,000 to the village of Lake George.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
